# Tests — FY26 Sales Commission Plan: clawback

Assertion-based tests for `Clawback.RecoverableCommission`. Every branch of
the `recoverable_amount` chain is covered — the `no_recovery` base, S-7.1,
S-7.2 and S-7.3 — and the 24-month long-stop in S-7.3 is tested on both sides
of the boundary, including the case where both S-7.2 and S-7.3 would apply,
which is the case that would raise a runtime `Conflict` if S-7.3 had been
encoded as a sibling of S-7.2 rather than below it.

The judgement input `terminated_for_company_material_breach` is supplied by
the test, never inferred: each test says what a human decided.

> Using Clawback

## The base case — no general right of recovery

A contract that has not become a Churned Contract yields nothing recoverable,
whatever was paid on it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestBase_NotChurnedNothingRecoverable:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestBase_NotChurnedNothingRecoverable:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $40,000
      -- payment_date: |2026-01-31|
      -- assessment_date: |2026-06-30|
      -- is_churned_contract: false
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: false
    }
  assertion r.recovery_time_barred = false
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $0
```

## S-7.1 Churn makes the commission recoverable

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS7_1_ChurnedRecoverable:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestS7_1_ChurnedRecoverable:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $40,000
      -- payment_date: |2026-01-31|
      -- assessment_date: |2026-06-30|
      -- is_churned_contract: true
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: false
    }
  assertion r.long_stop_date = |2028-01-31|
  assertion r.recovery_time_barred = false
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $40,000
```

The whole of the commission attributable to the contract is recoverable, not a
proportion of it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS7_1_WholeAttributableAmount:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestS7_1_WholeAttributableAmount:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $137.55
      -- payment_date: |2026-01-31|
      -- assessment_date: |2026-02-01|
      -- is_churned_contract: true
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: false
    }
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $137.55
```

## S-7.2 A material breach by the Company bars recovery

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS7_2_MaterialBreachBarsRecovery:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestS7_2_MaterialBreachBarsRecovery:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $40,000
      -- payment_date: |2026-01-31|
      -- assessment_date: |2026-06-30|
      -- is_churned_contract: true
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: true
    }
  assertion r.recovery_time_barred = false
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $0
```

S-7.2's condition repeats S-7.1's: on a contract that never churned, the
judgement that the Company was in material breach changes nothing, because no
right of recovery arose for it to defeat.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS7_2_BreachOnUnchurnedContract:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestS7_2_BreachOnUnchurnedContract:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $40,000
      -- payment_date: |2026-01-31|
      -- assessment_date: |2026-06-30|
      -- is_churned_contract: false
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: true
    }
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $0
```

## S-7.3 The 24-month long-stop, on both sides

The long-stop runs from the date the commission was **paid**. Commission paid
on 31 January 2026 may still be recovered on 31 January 2028: that is exactly
24 months after, and S-7.3 bars recovery only "more than" 24 months after.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS7_3_ExactlyTwentyFourMonths:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestS7_3_ExactlyTwentyFourMonths:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $40,000
      -- payment_date: |2026-01-31|
      -- assessment_date: |2028-01-31|
      -- is_churned_contract: true
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: false
    }
  assertion r.long_stop_date = |2028-01-31|
  assertion r.recovery_time_barred = false
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $40,000
```

One day later it is out of time.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS7_3_OneDayAfterTwentyFourMonths:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestS7_3_OneDayAfterTwentyFourMonths:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $40,000
      -- payment_date: |2026-01-31|
      -- assessment_date: |2028-02-01|
      -- is_churned_contract: true
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: false
    }
  assertion r.long_stop_date = |2028-01-31|
  assertion r.recovery_time_barred = true
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $0
```

The long-stop is measured from payment and not from signature or churn: a
churn event long inside the 180-day window of S-2.4 does not restart it. Here
the commission was paid on 1 October 2025 and the assessment is on 1 November
2027, which is more than 24 months after payment.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS7_3_MeasuredFromPaymentDate:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestS7_3_MeasuredFromPaymentDate:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $40,000
      -- payment_date: |2025-10-01|
      -- assessment_date: |2027-11-01|
      -- is_churned_contract: true
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: false
    }
  assertion r.long_stop_date = |2027-10-01|
  assertion r.recovery_time_barred = true
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $0
```

## S-7.3 sits below S-7.2, so the two bars cannot conflict

Both bars apply on these facts. Encoded as siblings they would be two
applicable definitions with neither an exception to the other, which is a
runtime `Conflict`. Encoded as a chain, S-7.3 governs and the answer is nil.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS7_3_BreachAndTimeBarredTogether:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestS7_3_BreachAndTimeBarredTogether:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $40,000
      -- payment_date: |2026-01-31|
      -- assessment_date: |2028-06-30|
      -- is_churned_contract: true
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: true
    }
  assertion r.recovery_time_barred = true
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $0
```

S-7.3 repeats S-7.1's condition but not S-7.2's: it applies whether or not
there was a material breach, and it does not reach a contract that never
churned.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS7_3_TimeBarredOnUnchurnedContract:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestS7_3_TimeBarredOnUnchurnedContract:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $40,000
      -- payment_date: |2026-01-31|
      -- assessment_date: |2028-06-30|
      -- is_churned_contract: false
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: false
    }
  assertion r.recovery_time_barred = true
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $0
```

## S-7.3 The leap-day long-stop

24 months after 29 February 2024 is a date that does not exist. `date round
down` puts the long-stop on 28 February 2026, which is the reading that does
not extend the Company's recovery window. Recovery on that day is in time.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS7_3_LeapDayLongStopInTime:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestS7_3_LeapDayLongStopInTime:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $40,000
      -- payment_date: |2024-02-29|
      -- assessment_date: |2026-02-28|
      -- is_churned_contract: true
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: false
    }
  assertion r.long_stop_date = |2026-02-28|
  assertion r.recovery_time_barred = false
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $40,000
```

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestS7_3_LeapDayLongStopOutOfTime:
  output r content Clawback.RecoverableCommission

scope TestS7_3_LeapDayLongStopOutOfTime:
  definition r equals
    output of Clawback.RecoverableCommission with {
      -- commission_paid: $40,000
      -- payment_date: |2024-02-29|
      -- assessment_date: |2026-03-01|
      -- is_churned_contract: true
      -- terminated_for_company_material_breach: false
    }
  assertion r.long_stop_date = |2026-02-28|
  assertion r.recovery_time_barred = true
  assertion r.recoverable_amount = $0
```
